WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.970
High in the mountain forests of
tropical Africa grows an evergreen tree:

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:08.030
Prunus africana, the African cherry.

3
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.130
It typically grows between
900 and 3,400 metres up.

4
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:17.590
Its bark is stripped, shipped abroad,
and made into an extract for men with an

5
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.410
enlarged prostate.

6
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.730
Researchers report that no African tree
species has been more widely exported

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:24.850
for medicine.

8
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.690
So can that trade last,
without losing the tree?

9
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.210
In this mission, you'll see how climate
and soil decide where medicinal plants

10
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.570
grow, and test whether this bark works.

11
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.430
Then you'll weigh the threats to the tree,

12
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.070
and judge which ways
of using it could last.

13
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.600
Your mission: decide whether the bark
trade can last without losing the tree.
